{"id": "sevt_01LGDgPkyZnfPYAiPWUBmn6r", "content": [{"text": "**Finding: the checkout deploy `0860430` (14:09:42Z) replaced a batched order-items query with one query per open order, and p99 moved with it.**\n\nEvidence, in runbook order:\n\n1. **Deploys (last 6h):** The only checkout deploy is `0860430` by alice, at 14:09:42Z. The cart deploy `f552945` at 14:33:05Z is after the spike and doesn't match it.\n2. **Timing:** `checkout` p99 was 75 ms at 14:08 and 2090 ms at 14:09, then 3965 ms at 14:10. It kept climbing to about 6000 ms by 14:59. The deploy comes about 5 seconds before the first per-row query in the log (14:09:47.994Z), and the jump appears in the 14:09 bucket.\n3. **Diff:** The commit is labeled a readability refactor, but it changes `build_summary` from one `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id__in=ids)` query, grouped in memory, to `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id=order.order_id)` inside a loop. That is one query per open order, which is the \"per-row query where there used to be a batch\" pattern from the runbook.\n4. **Log confirmation:**\n   - Before 14:09, every order_items query was the batched `IN (...)` form, 3 to 7 per minute.\n   - From 14:09:47 on, per-row queries ran at about 100 to 125 per minute, with no batch queries after that point.\n   - Each individual query is fast (about 13 ms), so the cost is the multiplication by the number of orders per request, which adds DB round trips to every checkout summary.\n   - Later, the log shows `DB connection pool exhausted (active=50/50, waiters=12)` and `PoolTimeout` 500s on `/api/checkout/validate` from 14:18 onward. These are the downstream effect of the same N+1 pattern holding connections longer.\n\nCaveats: the dashboard `error_rate` stays under about 0.6%, but the log has 244 ERROR lines, nearly all pool timeouts. I did not check `db_pool_utilization` across services, since a deploy lines up and the runbook doesn't call for that check. The fix is to revert `0860430` or restore the batched query. Confidence is high on the mechanism; I did not roll back or verify a fix.\n\n**Root cause:** `0860430` \u2014 the \"readability\" refactor changed a single batched `order_items` query into one query per open order, so each checkout summary issues N extra DB round trips, which raised p99 from about 75 ms to 2\u20136 s and exhausted the DB connection pool.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T11:51:05.608411Z", "type": "agent.message"}
